# BJS File Compilation Rule

## Important: Do Not Edit Vala Files Directly

**NEVER** edit `.vala` files that have corresponding `.bjs` files with the same name. These Vala files are **generated** and will be overwritten.

**CRITICAL**: Before editing ANY `.vala` file, ALWAYS check if a corresponding `.bjs` file exists. If it does, edit the `.bjs` file instead and compile it to generate the `.vala` file.

## BJS Compilation Process

Files with `.bjs` extensions need to be compiled using the roobuilder tool before the corresponding Vala files can be used.

### Compilation Command

```bash
/usr/bin/roobuilder --project /home/alan/gitlive/roobuilder --test-symbol-target roobuilder --test-bjs-compile src/Builder4/MainWindow.bjs > /tmp/generated_mainwindow.vala
```

### General Pattern

```bash
/usr/bin/roobuilder --project /home/alan/gitlive/roobuilder --test-symbol-target roobuilder --test-bjs-compile [BJS_FILE_PATH] > /tmp/generated_[filename].vala
```

### Handling File Structure Dumps

**Important**: Sometimes the BJS compiler output includes a file structure dump at the beginning. If the output starts with `File /...` (indicating a file path), this means the compiler is showing file changes and the output is not clean Vala code.

**Solution**: Run the compiler **twice**:
1. **First run**: May include file structure dump
2. **Second run**: Should produce clean Vala code

```bash
# First compilation (may include file structure dump)
/usr/bin/roobuilder --project /home/alan/gitlive/roobuilder --test-symbol-target roobuilder --test-bjs-compile src/Builder4/MainWindow.bjs > /tmp/generated_mainwindow.vala

# Check if output starts with "File /" - if so, run again
head -1 /tmp/generated_mainwindow.vala | grep -q "^File /" && \
/usr/bin/roobuilder --project /home/alan/gitlive/roobuilder --test-symbol-target roobuilder --test-bjs-compile src/Builder4/MainWindow.bjs > /tmp/generated_mainwindow.vala

# Now copy the clean output
cp /tmp/generated_mainwindow.vala src/Builder4/MainWindow.vala
```

