## Workflow for BJS Files

1. **Edit the .bjs file** - Make your changes in the BJS source
2. **Compile using roobuilder** - Run the compilation command
3. **Copy generated code** - Copy from `/tmp/generated_[filename].vala` to the actual Vala file
4. **Test compilation** - Ensure the project builds correctly

## Example Workflow

```bash
# 1. Edit the BJS file
vim src/Builder4/MainWindow.bjs

# 2. Compile it (first attempt)
/usr/bin/roobuilder --project /home/alan/gitlive/roobuilder --test-symbol-target roobuilder --test-bjs-compile src/Builder4/MainWindow.bjs > /tmp/generated_mainwindow.vala

# 3. Check if output is clean (no file structure dump)
if head -1 /tmp/generated_mainwindow.vala | grep -q "^File /"; then
    # Output contains file structure dump, compile again
    /usr/bin/roobuilder --project /home/alan/gitlive/roobuilder --test-symbol-target roobuilder --test-bjs-compile src/Builder4/MainWindow.bjs > /tmp/generated_mainwindow.vala
fi

# 4. Copy the generated code
cp /tmp/generated_mainwindow.vala src/Builder4/MainWindow.vala

# 5. Build the project
meson compile -C build
```

## Code Review Guidelines

When reviewing changes:

1. **Check for BJS pairs** - If a Vala file has a corresponding BJS file, ensure changes were made to the BJS file
2. **Verify compilation** - Ensure the BJS file compiles correctly
3. **Look for manual edits** - Flag any direct edits to generated Vala files
4. **Check consistency** - Ensure BJS and Vala files are in sync

## Common Mistakes to Avoid

### ❌ Wrong Approach
```bash
# DON'T edit Vala files directly
vim src/Builder4/MainWindow.vala  # This will be overwritten!
```

### ✅ Correct Approach
```bash
# DO edit BJS files and compile them
vim src/Builder4/MainWindow.bjs
/usr/bin/roobuilder --project /home/alan/gitlive/roobuilder --test-symbol-target roobuilder --test-bjs-compile src/Builder4/MainWindow.bjs > /tmp/generated_mainwindow.vala
cp /tmp/generated_mainwindow.vala src/Builder4/MainWindow.vala
```

